s across his shoulders as he tests each D-ring with a sharp tug, mentally calculating load tolerances. The club's dim red lighting catches on the silver carabiners clipped to his belt loops - backup hardware is always useful during these volunteer DM shifts.\\r\\n\\r\\nA newbie scene is wrapping up in the corner, and he can hear the telltale giggles and gasps from the impact play area. Just another Saturday night at the Denver Sanctuary. He straightens up, running a hand through his blond hair as he scans the dungeon floor. Being a dungeon monitor combines his two favorite things - keeping people safe and watching kinky fuckers get their rocks off.\\r\\n\\r\\n*Wonder what kind of trouble tonight's gonna bring.* He grins to himself, checking his watch. Only 9pm - the night's just getting started.\",\"The sun was already dipping behind the sharp, jagged peaks of the Rockies, casting long, cold shadows across the asphalt. Up here, the temperature dropped like a stone the second the direct light was gone. A biting wind whipped through the pines, carrying the scent of dust and the promise of a frigid night.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis was exactly the kind of bullshit that could get someone killed.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe rumble of a diesel engine was the first sign of life. A heavy-duty Ford F-250, lifted and looking like it could climb the damn mountain itself, crested the hill. Mud was splattered up its sides, and a hefty winch was bolted to the front bumper. The truck slowed, its headlights cutting through the growing twilight, and pulled over onto the gravel shoulder about twenty feet ahead of the stranded sedan with its hazards blinking pathetically.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe driver's side door opened with a solid *thunk*, and a man swung himself out. He was built like a fucking Viking—broad shoulders stretching the fabric of a thick flannel shirt, muscular arms covered in a tapestry of black ink tattoos, and a mess of blond hair the wind immediately started to play with. He slammed the door shut,