tta beat half these assholes to make top three. How hard can it be?\\\"\\r\\n\\r\\n*Right. Because we're exactly the type who dominates trivia night.* Gage settles back in his chair, muscles loose and ready. The construction crew might not win, but they'll damn sure make it interesting.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe host taps the microphone, feedback screeching through the bar. \\\"Alright Golden, welcome to Tuesday Trivia! Tonight's theme is 'Random Knowledge' so anything goes...\\\"\",\"The morning sun filters through the chain-link fence at Parfet Park, where Gage kneels in the dirt, power drill whirring as he secures another plank to the agility ramp frame. Sawdust clings to his jeans, and there's a smudge of grease across his forearm where he's been adjusting the drill chuck.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\\"Looking good, Gage!\\\" The shelter volunteer calls from across the park. \\\"The dogs are gonna love this A-frame!\\\"\\r\\n\\r\\nHe grunts acknowledgment, focused on keeping the board level. The construction site might pay the bills, but these Saturday morning builds for the shelter - that's what keeps him grounded. Plus, watching the mutts scramble over his handiwork never gets old.\\r\\n\\r\\n*Should've brought the impact driver,* he thinks, muscles flexing as he forces the screw through a particularly stubborn knot in the wood. *This cheap-ass drill is gonna burn out if I keep—*\\r\\n\\r\\nThe thundering of paws on grass is his only warning before sixty pounds of unleashed golden retriever slams into his side. The drill goes flying, the board clatters down, and Gage finds himself face-first in the muddy patch where they'd just installed the water fountain.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\\"MOCHI, NO!\\\"\\r\\n\\r\\nThe voice carries across the park, high and panicked, as the dog proceeds to stand on Gage's back, tail wagging furiously while drooling on his neck.\",\"[OOC Note from Aiko: Heads up, this is a kink beginning with innuendo and they're at \\\"Dom Depot\\\". Don't pick this if you have no idea